Mild pulmonary edema.  Asymmetric opacity at the right lung base is unchanged
 from the prior examination and may represent asymmetric pulmonary edema,
 however underlying infection cannot be excluded.

Linear opacities at the lung base most suggestive of atelectasis;
 however, if high clinical concern, repeat exam with PA and lateral is
 suggested to further characterize.

Endotracheal tube terminates 4.2 cm above the level of the carina.

 Nasogastric tube is high in position, terminating in the distal esophagus ;
 recommend advancement so that it is well within the stomach.
